{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synchronization context and configure await synchronization context and configure await","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","fileName":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synchronization context and configure await synchronization context and configure await","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","fileName":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait","heading":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A synchronization context can capture where an awaited method should resume, such as a user-interface thread that owns controls. This preserves thread-affine behavior but adds scheduling work and can participate in deadlock when a caller blocks that same context waiting for completion.\n\n`ConfigureAwait(false)` tells an await not to require the captured context for its continuation. It is useful in reusable library code that does not need thread-affine state, while application code must retain the context when subsequent work actually depends on it.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synchronization context and configure await synchronization context and configure await","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","fileName":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SynchronizationContext and ConfigureAwait","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}